            <ArticleTitle>[Effectiveness of Sacral Intervertebral Epidural Block for Umbilical Hernia Repair in Children].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>150-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Effectiveness of sacral intervertebral epidural block (S 2-3 block) for umbilical hernia repair has not been clarified.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">We investigate 24 children, undergoing umbilical hernia repair; mean age of 3 years (age range: 20-65 months). Under general anesthesia, epidural block was performed at S 2-3 interspace with 1 ml x kg(-1) ropivacaine (0.2%) at injecting rate of 1 ml x sec(-1) followed by 0.25 ml x kg(-1) normal saline.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">In all cases, neither systolic blood pressure nor heart rate increased &gt; 15% from those just before the block. Postoperative analgesics were given in 6 patients (25%) rectally. Mean time between the block and the administration of analgesic was 10.5 hours.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">S 2-3 block can be effective for postoperative pain in umbilical hernia repair.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
